From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:32:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: count what each command buffer holds and each upload site
 asks for

With MESA_KK_DEBUG=memory (the dev app's default), log every 30 s, from
the [kk-mem] line, a [kk-cmd-census] of the command buffers alive:

- one line with their count, how many hold a recording, the upload BOs
  and allocator bytes those recordings hold, the allocators' total,
  largest and count over 8 MiB, the direct and replayed submits of
  reusable (not ONE_TIME) primaries, and the application's recordings
  released so far by how long they held after their first submit (or
  never submitted), with the MiB they held;
- up to twelve buckets holding the most: queue re-record or the
  application's, level, usage (once, simultaneous, reusable), pool flags
  (transient, reset), and state (recording, ended-unsubmitted,
  submitted-once, submitted-2+), each with its count, upload and
  allocator MiB, and ages (since the first submit, else since Begin).

A recording holds from Begin to kk_cmd_release_resources (reset, free or
the next Begin). What it added to its allocator is allocatedSize at End
less at Begin: an allocator records one buffer at a time.

Then [kk-upload]: every kk_pool_alloc and kk_pool_upload counts at its
caller's site (a macro gives each a static record), with requests and
bytes, and for requests over 128 KiB the bytes asked, the power-of-two
heap bytes given, and those still owned by a command buffer. One line of
totals, then the twelve sites with the most bytes.

Every count sits behind KK_DEBUG(MEMORY) or the buffer's listing, which
is made only then. No allocation, release, reset or encoding changes.
kk-cmd-census-test.c checks the lines on the mock.

Linear: PLA-364
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-30-rdr2-kk-audio-diagnostics.md
Offered-upstream: no
